Package: frmtmb.spatial
Title: Spatial Random Fields for 'frmtmb' Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Alex", "Forrence", email = "alex.forrence@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9728-6337"))
Description: Spatial random fields for 'frmtmb' models, registered with
    'frmtmb' through its public covariance-structure seam. car() is the
    conditional autoregressive field of 'brms', over an adjacency matrix,
    in its four types: the proper CAR, the intrinsic CAR under an exact or
    a soft sum-to-zero constraint, and the scaled BYM2 mixture of Riebler
    et al. (2016). spde() is a Matern field over a finite-element mesh,
    through the stochastic partial differential equation representation
    of Lindgren, Rue and Lindstrom (2011), taking the mesh's matrices as
    fixed data. Each is fitted by maximum likelihood with the field
    integrated out by the Laplace approximation, which is exact for a
    gaussian response.
